{"_id":"68a736128ec3d8323af14731","roadmapSlug":"data-analyst","nodeId":"2ldO-_ZnIg364Eo8Jyfgr","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:58.099Z","description":"# Dispersion\n\nDispersion measures how spread out values are in a dataset. High dispersion means values vary widely; low dispersion means they cluster close to the center. Range, variance, and standard deviation are the primary measures of dispersion.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is dispersion?","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/dispersion.asp","_id":"6a7f4a4fcb44947debcf5a3d"},{"type":"video","title":"Statistics 101 - Measures of Dispersion","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=goXdWMZxlqM","_id":"6a7f4a4fcb44947debcf5a3e"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:03:11.488Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a8894ecaca636c6b9e973f1","title":"DataCamp - Associate Data Analyst in SQL","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/1GK1qD"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041675b","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/AgYmJK"},{"_id":"6a5e189a077863512aba4c73","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/data-analyst/content/2ldO-_ZnIg364Eo8Jyfgr.md"}